==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*glewbʰ-}}
From {{der|en|la|gluma||husk of grain}}. The root can also be seen in {{m|la|glubere||to peel}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|en|uːm|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|botany}} A [[basal]], [[membranous]], outer [[sterile]] [[husk]] or [[bract]] in the flowers of grasses ([[Poaceae]]) and [[sedge]]s ([[Cyperaceae]]).
#*'''1789''', {{w|Erasmus Darwin}}, ''The Loves of the Plants'', J. Johnson, p. 9:
#*:[T]he '''glume''' in some alpine grasses, and the scales of the ament in the salix rosea, rose-willow, grow into leaves; and produce other kinds of monsters.

